'' T33, RUN: under -exx, reading 'p->y' through a null pointer is runtime error 7, exit 7,
'' as fbc reports it -- it checks the base pointer of every '->'. tiko checked '*p' and
'' '(*p).y' but not the arrow, so the program segfaulted. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/nullchk-arrow-read.bas -o tests/codegen/nullchkarrowread.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/nullchkarrowread.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/nullchkarrowread.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: runtime error 7 (null pointer access) at line 7 of
